{
  "Title": "ELSA-2026-102191:  openssh security, bug fix, and enhancement update (MODERATE)",
  "Description": "[9.9p1-17.0.1]\n- Restore pam_ssh_agent_rel values that were used for initial release\n- Fix PerSourcePenalties grace-exceeded using the crash penalty value [Orabug: 39825354]\n- Replace unsupported ML-KEM hybrid algorithm skip logic with v9.9p1-23.el10_2 ML-KEM/NIST backport [Orabug: 39423076]\n- Upstream references found with /usr/bin/ssh [Orabug: 37814929]\n\n[9.9p1-17]\n- CVE-2026-106552: Fix arbitrary file write via directory traversal\n  during sftp recursive copy\n  Resolves: RHEL-286928\n- CVE-2026-106585: Fix DoS via oversized decompressed packets\n  Resolves: RHEL-286938\n- CVE-2026-106583: Fix command injection via unvalidated command-line username\n  Resolves: RHEL-286961\n- CVE-2026-106582: Fix compression side-channel by disabling L77 dictionary coder\n  Resolves: RHEL-286931\n- CVE-2026-106553: Fix credentials persisting after GSSAPI authentication attempt failure\n  Resolves: RHEL-286887\n- Fix resource leaks in krb5 and GSSAPI authentication\n  Related: RHEL-286887\n- Fix and enable the PKCS#11 URI tests\n  Related: RHEL-288511\n- Restores functionality of IdentitiesOnly=yes with PKCS#11 URI in IdentityFile\n  Resolves: RHEL-288511",
  "Platform": [
    "Oracle Linux 9"
  ],
